{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nJira fix versions now reach rebar, but a rebar release never reaches Jira: no outbound diff compares `releases` and no transport writes fix versions. This child implements rebar→Jira per ADR 0124 (decisions 5, 6), following tags→labels, for both adapters.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Transport.** Add `add_fix_version(remote_id, name)`/`remove_fix_version(remote_id, name)` to the `TicketTransport` protocol in `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py` (beside `add_label`/`remove_label`) and to `_REQUIRED_TRANSPORT_MEMBERS`, so the conformance guard covers them. Per-item verbs only, never `set`:\n   - Cloud (`adapters/jira/acli_graph.py`, beside `add_label`): `self._direct_rest_put_raw(f\"/rest/api/3/issue/{key}\", {\"update\": {\"fixVersions\": [{\"add\": {\"name\": name}}]}})`; remove uses `{\"remove\": {\"name\": name}}`. Non-2xx raises `HTTPError`.\n   - DC (`adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`, beside `remove_label`): `issue.update(update={\"fixVersions\": [{\"add\": {\"name\": name}}]})`, through `_call_logged` as `remove_label` does.\n   - Test transports with `remove_label` gain both verbs: `tests/unit/reconciler/backend_support.py`, `apply/_sync_only_dispatch_probe.py`, `mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py`, `mutate/test_outbound_update_combined.py`, `orchestrate/test_e2e_dedup_pass.py`, `orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py`, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py`; `test_transport_port_completeness.py`'s `_REQUIRED` lists them. Write-method inventories gain both names: `_CLASSIFIED_MUTATING` in `test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep.py`, the `mutations` dict in `test_dc_rate_limit_retry.py`, and `MUTATING_TRANSPORT_METHODS` in `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/_cloud_s3_support.py`.\n2. **Intent.** In `local_label_intent.py` add `compute_release_intent_map(bound_local_ids, tracker_dir)`: names from non-inbound `RELEASE_DELTA.added` and `SNAPSHOT.compiled_state.releases` (ADR 0124 decision 5); `source == \"inbound\"` deltas are skipped and `.removed` is never folded, as for tags. Known limit shared with labels: after compaction a SNAPSHOT folds inbound-origin names into intent. `outbound_pass.py` computes it beside `compute_label_intent_map` and passes `local_release_intent` on `OutboundDiffConfig`.\n3. **Diff.** New `outbound_releases.py` with `_diff_releases(ticket, jira_fields, intent_set)`, mirroring `outbound_labels._diff_labels`: names come from `inbound_collection_diffs._jira_release_names`; a non-list `fixVersions` yields `[]`; ADD a local name missing in Jira and REMOVE a Jira name missing locally, each only when the name is in `intent_set` (bug a06c). Records are `{\"action\", \"release\"}`.\n4. **Mutation and payload.** Add `releases` to `OutboundMutation`, call `_diff_releases` in the bound-update builder (`outbound_mutation_builders._compute_outbound_update_mutation`), and include it in the emit condition and `RECON: outbound_update` log. In `mutation_payloads.OutboundUpdatePayload` add `releases` to the fields, `_OUTBOUND_UPDATE_KEYS`, the non-empty check, `as_legacy_dict` (emitted only when non-empty, so existing outbound manifests and the canonical manifest hash are unchanged) and `from_legacy`. `outbound_pass.py` passes `releases=tuple(getattr(om, \"releases\", []))`; `batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict` reads `typed.releases` / `payload.get(\"releases\", [])` and emits `\"releases\"`.\n5. **Dispatch.** Add `_update_one_dispatch_releases(mutation, client, issue_key)` in `dispatch_one.py`, mirroring `_update_one_dispatch_labels`: per item, failures logged to stderr (for `urllib.error.HTTPError`, with up to 500 bytes of Jira's error body) and retried next pass; returns computed/applied counts, added to `subop_applied` as `releases_computed`/`releases_applied`. `apply_handlers.py` exposes `releases_applied` and adds `\"releases\"` to the silent-no-op canary kinds.\n6. **Suppression.** Already wired by the inbound child.\n7. **Create path.** A Jira issue created from a rebar ticket gets its releases on the next bound-update pass; the create payload is unchanged.\n8. **Docs.** In `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` mark the fix-versions outbound cell supported (per-item add/remove), with a \"pending live verification (ADR 0124; production check is plucky-jetblack-parrot)\" note: the version must already exist in the Jira project, and Fix versions may need to be on the project's edit screen.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/`: `_backend.py`, `adapters/jira/acli_graph.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`, `local_label_intent.py`, `outbound_releases.py` (new), `outbound_differ.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_pass.py`, `mutation_payloads.py`, `batch_dispatch.py`, `dispatch_one.py`, `apply_handlers.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- New tests: `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py`, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py`\n- Extended tests: `mutate/test_local_label_intent.py`, `test_field_contract_properties.py`, `mutate/test_mutation_payloads.py`, `test_transport_port_completeness.py`, `test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep.py`, `test_dc_rate_limit_retry.py`, `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/_cloud_s3_support.py`, and the 7 test transports in step 1\n\n## Testing\n\n- Transport: Cloud add sends `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/REB-1` with `{\"update\":{\"fixVersions\":[{\"add\":{\"name\":\"2.4\"}}]}}` (captured `urllib` request); remove sends `{\"remove\":{\"name\":\"2.4\"}}`; a 400 raises `HTTPError`. DC calls `issue.update(update=...)` with the same item on a fake pycontribs issue. Neither sends `set` or `fields.fixVersions`.\n- Diff: local `[\"2.4\"]`, Jira `[]`, 2.4 in intent → add; not in intent → `[]`; local `[]`, Jira `[\"2.4\"]`, in intent → remove; not in intent → `[]`; unobserved → `[]`.\n- Intent: an inbound `RELEASE_DELTA` adds nothing; a local delta's added names and SNAPSHOT releases are included; removed names are not.\n- Payload: `OutboundUpdatePayload` round-trips with and without releases, and a releases-free payload projects no `releases` key; a releases-only payload is valid; `_mutation_to_batch_dict` carries releases.\n- Dispatch: one failing write logs the Jira error body and the next item still runs; computed > 0 with applied 0 trips the silent-no-op canary.\n- Suppression: a real `OutboundMutation` adding 2.4 drops the inbound REMOVE of 2.4.\n- Round trip (integration, Cloud- and DC-shaped fakes): a local add pushes one add, then a no-op pass writes nothing; a local remove of a locally added release pushes one remove; a Jira-side add arrives as one `RELEASE_DELTA`; a Jira-side removal of an inbound-origin name gives one inbound remove and zero Jira writes; a new issue gets its release on the pass after create.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A local release add produces exactly one per-item `fixVersions` add on the next pass, on Cloud and DC; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Removing a locally added release produces exactly one per-item `fixVersions` remove; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Cloud and DC request bodies match the bodies above; pinned by the transport test.\n- [ ] A Jira fix version rebar never held is never removed; pinned by the diff test.\n- [ ] A Jira-side removal of an inbound-origin release on an uncompacted ticket is not undone; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] A pass with no change writes no Jira update and no rebar event; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Release records reach `update_one` through `outbound_pass` and `batch_dispatch`; pinned by the payload test.\n- [ ] Existing outbound manifest shapes are unchanged; pinned by the existing manifest tests.\n- [ ] Existing label outbound and dispatch tests pass unchanged.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] No `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794376460407399675,"uuid":"6195e5b5-6ab1-4ea4-ae75-b402b46b45e5"}